## 6. Import Update Strategy

All files use the `@/` path alias (mapped to `src/`) — no relative imports are broken by restructuring. The update approach:

1. **Move file** → **update the file's own imports** (if it imports siblings that also moved)
2. **Global find-and-replace** the old `@/` path with the new `@/features/...` path
3. **[main.tsx](file:///c:/Users/Administrator/Videos/alikohub-v2/domains/academy/lms/src/main.tsx)**: Update [App](file:///c:/Users/Administrator/Videos/alikohub-v2/domains/academy/lms/src/App.tsx#144-157) import from `@/App` → `@/app/App`
4. **[App.tsx](file:///c:/Users/Administrator/Videos/alikohub-v2/domains/academy/lms/src/App.tsx)**: Most imports change since all pages are moving

> [!TIP]
> Because every import uses `@/` (absolute alias), moving files does NOT break sibling imports. Only the *import statements pointing to the moved file* need updating.

